*> PLB-C111 sort-statement-wrong-phase: RETURN in a SORT's INPUT
*> PROCEDURE, or RELEASE in an OUTPUT PROCEDURE.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SORTPHASE.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN TO "SORTWK".
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
SD  SORT-FILE.
01  SORT-REC            PIC X(10).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-EOF              PIC X VALUE "N".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    SORT SORT-FILE ON ASCENDING KEY SORT-REC
        INPUT PROCEDURE IS LOAD-RECORDS
        OUTPUT PROCEDURE IS WRITE-RECORDS THRU WRITE-EXIT
    STOP RUN.
LOAD-RECORDS.
    MOVE "B" TO SORT-REC
    RELEASE SORT-REC
    *> Reported: RETURN in the input procedure.
    RETURN SORT-FILE AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF END-RETURN.
WRITE-RECORDS.
    RETURN SORT-FILE AT END MOVE "Y" TO WS-EOF END-RETURN
    PERFORM ADD-TRAILER.
WRITE-EXIT.
    EXIT.
ADD-TRAILER.
    *> Reported: RELEASE in a paragraph the output procedure performs.
    MOVE "ZZZ" TO SORT-REC
    RELEASE SORT-REC.
